# deal_with_galaxy_merger with R2's flags, merge_r2_snap63_minor's galaxies with each
# galaxy's H2gas and H1gas stale at its whole cold gas: the addition sums the cold gas but
# not H2gas or H1gas (M:456-543), so the target keeps its own stale values, and the black-hole
# growth then caps both at the hydrogen of the target's remaining cold gas (M:366-372), before
# the wind and the burst's caps and refresh.
# Source: R2 reference /Volumes/Internal/results/sage26-campaign/workspace/e01-reference/out/R2/model_0.hdf5 (SHA-256 c6af6c9385d41adcccbd5f19e064323486706b0965183f61ebded290331f6714), Snap_63 rows 14849 (GalaxyIndex 3000165000000000, Type 0) and 14850 (GalaxyIndex 3000165000000011, Type 1).
# End-of-snapshot output values used as plausible call inputs, not reconstructed call-time
# state; the writer stores every galaxy field below verbatim (R/src/io/save_gals_hdf5.c:895-1005;
# DiskScaleRadius is the output's DiskRadius), the bulge radii included.
# Constructed: the galaxies' SnapNum (one less than the row's), deltaMvir (central +2% of
# Mvir, satellite -5%), the clocks (999.9 for the central, B:288; 0.0 for the satellite,
# unread), OutflowRate 0, TimeOfLast*Merger -1 (SAGE26's creation sentinel), zero histories,
# and the call time, dt and bin (the R1 template's: the last bin of the substeps).
# Reachability: constructed routine-domain probe (the stale H2gas and H1gas).
format sage26-oracle-fixture 1
